An unordered, forward-facing backlog; completed work and its rationale
live in the git history of this file, docs/plans/, docs/design/, and
NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Every item has an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md,
and the planning/implementation/review process (who plans, who
implements, who reviews, which gates run) is docs/plans/README.md.
"window: pre-release" marks items whose cheap form expires when 1.0-0
freezes the R and dbarts.h compatibility contracts: they need a
go/no-go decision before submission, not necessarily the work itself.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  blocked-jacobi-trees: exact parallel tree updates via noise-splitting
    augmentation (per-tree pseudo-responses y_k ~ N(g_k, sigma^2/b),
    sum-constrained): b trees update independently per barrier at the
    cost of b-fold precision on structure moves. The single-chain
    parallelism candidate; an ESS-per-second experiment decides
    (protocol and the memory-wall bound:
    docs/design/within-chain-threading.md). low-ranked.
  forest-ranef-interweaving: the grouped-fit mixing bottleneck is
    forest-ranef confounding, not the tau draw (measurements and
    ranked remedies: docs/plans/tau-slice-review.md). Candidates: a
    joint/interweaving move between the forest fit and the random
    intercepts (design from scratch), or ASIS on (tau, b)
    (prototype-gate: partial in the full engine). Needs a measurement
    harness (grouped SBC or IACT grid) before any engine work.
    decision-gated.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  gpu-bart: backend-seam design waits on frontier items 4-5
    (informed-kernel + CG-leaf prototypes); memo and falsifiers in
    docs/design/gpu-bart.md and parallel-bart-frontier.md.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: frontier 3.1's exact informed-proposal use of the
    shared scan.
  interaction-constraints: structured sparsity and interaction limits
    on the SplitSelector seam. consumer-gated.
  monotone-bart: shape-constrained fits via the tree-level leaf-draw
    hook the design provisioned.
  multi-forest-models: multinomial, heteroscedastic, hurdle - the BCF
    two-forest machinery is the template; one design note each when
    picked. forest-combiner (docs/design/forest-combiner.md) LANDED
    2026-07-14 and discharges the coupling-seam prerequisite; each
    note still has to plan against the Chain-level re-carves it names
    (a single combined-fit location, a single response_/sigma_, a
    single-leaf-type forest vector, a BCF-shaped state wire format).
    heteroscedastic additionally needs a fourth leaf kind
    (multiplicative-positive, non-integrable) plus the non-conjugate
    MoveStrategy the design anticipated but never built, and a
    decision on per-observation residual variance (fold into the
    workingWeights channel vs a sigma vector).
  mutation-journal: build-new-and-swap for setPredictor instead of
    copy-old-and-restore; cell-granular journal for the patch paths;
    document the cost contract per entry point.
  negative-binomial: count outcomes via the Polya-Gamma NB
    augmentation (the PG sampler already ships); the r update decides
    integer vs real shape - a caveat shared with weighted-binary.
  ordinal-outcomes: cumulative probit on the existing truncated-normal
    machinery plus a cutpoint block.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge; a pybind11 facade wrapper becomes prototype-scale. horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. decision-gated.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Remaining: PR-gate the
    sanitizers workflow once the new gcc-asan/valgrind legs prove
    stable on pushes; optional codecov badge (VD's call); optional
    roxygen2 and NEWS.md migrations (do not start unasked).
  robust-errors: Student-t residuals as a scale-mixture on the
    workingWeights hook; composes with user weights.
  sparse-extensions: in-place nonzero mutation, streaming range kernel,
    mutation on dense-backed mixed columns (sparse-columns.md landing
    notes). consumer-gated.
  survival-models: discrete-time hazard (person-period ingestion over
    the binary families; design docs/design/survival.md).
  warm-starts: the cross-grid remap over mapOldCutPointsOntoNew;
    reopen when a consumer needs new-data warm starts.
  weighted-binary: post 1.0 - integer-weight probit via replicated
    latents; arbitrary real weights need a real-shape PG sampler (IPW
    is a pseudo-likelihood trap).
  x86-simd: three linalg SSE2/AVX bodies are scalar with intrinsics
    commented out (predates the rewrite; the originals used
    non-temporal stores autovectorization cannot emit) - measure on
    x86, restore or delete; add misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant to the
    dispatch table; SSR SIMD leaf; Windows-arm64 NEON config.

release (deferred; the one ordered procedure, run when VD triggers it)
  note: the schedule/dispatch-only workflows (equivalence, rchk,
    revdep-smoke) cannot register or run until they exist on the
    default branch - GitHub binds schedules and dispatch to it. Their
    first live runs happen when bartcore merges to main; validate them
    then.
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-13; submit both
    to CRAN together. bartCause is ready on branch dbarts-1.0 in
    ~/Repositories/bartCause (two commits, unpushed, checks Status OK):
    push and submit it after dbarts is accepted.
  before submission, resolve the window: pre-release decisions above
    (family-on-model, flat-format-v2 reporting, range-scaling,
    state-format-policy) - a documented "no" is a valid resolution.
  re-run the revdep sweep near submission (manual; the revdepcheck
    package is GitHub-only). 23 CRAN reverse dependencies; the last
    full pass was clean or explained everywhere (stan4bart 0.0-13 dev
    OK; bartMan/EBcoBART/funcml/glossa/nlfh/riAFTBART/voi OK with
    _R_CHECK_FORCE_SUGGESTS_=false; bartCause handled by its update;
    tidytreatment's WARNING is the documented ABI break, resolved by
    stan4bart 0.0-13; bartXViz not checkable locally - own gfortran
    runtime, R-level dbarts use only; the 12 Suggests-level packages
    not individually checked).
  write cran-comments.md at submission time. Content it needs: major
    release, engine rewritten, seeded results change; the C++ interface
    is removed and dbarts.h replaces it, so stan4bart 0.0-12 cannot
    build against 1.0-0 and 0.0-13 is submitted alongside (same
    maintainer); revdep summary as above; test environments; goal
    0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 notes.
  stan4bart follow-up: adopt categorical splits (it pins factors =
    "indicators"); lockstep with the dbarts release.
  optional courtesy: notify the tmle maintainers. Their default
    SuperLearner dbarts wrappers pass obsWeights unconditionally and
    pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled dbarts-side now, but
    genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts learners by
    design, and family routing on their side would need the matching
    inverse link.
